- BattleBallistics.h/.cpp (new, spec ranged-stack sections 4.1-4.3): the ONE
  low-arc launch solver (discriminant-root selection; out-of-envelope holds
  fire, RC2), PerturbDirection (deterministic cone-disc dispersion,
  rejection-free; bounded by construction), ShotSeed (the A13 run-invariant
  seed -- same Knuth family as FMeleeMath, cross-referenced per the B-2
  one-home posture), StepProjectile (semi-implicit Euler, the
  IntegrateProcessor family), MarchClear (sub-cell deduped DDA over the
  heightfield; strictly-greater occlusion so equal heights never block, RC3).
- FBattleCostGrid::SampleHeight (the ONLY grid change, disclosed in the spec
  touch-point table): bilinear world-space height; flat grids read exactly 0
  (flags-off baseline untouched).
- MassBattleRangedTests.cpp (new): T3.1 Battle.Unit.Ranged.Ballistics (45deg
  hand golden; stepped-landing property at both profile speeds with the
  discretization band documented; out-of-envelope; flatness monotonicity RC2;
  bit determinism; dispersion cone bound + per-seed determinism) + T3.2
  Battle.Unit.Ranged.LOS (flat never false-occludes; hill blocks; bump
  clears; equal-height epsilon rule; rising-lane over/under a mid-hill;
  bilinear SampleHeight goldens; march determinism).

MUST re-run on the UE machine: unit tier (the two new tests green; FMA
contraction on the same machine is the known watch item -- tolerances are
1e-3 analytic / 0.35 m stepped). Static patch: brace-balanced,
include-complete; no engine build was available at author time.
